WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.110
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for the child who guesses at words.

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.478
Here is a word.

3
00:00:05.878 --> 00:00:09.089
A child who guesses looks at the first letter, and says cat.

4
00:00:09.789 --> 00:00:13.739
The goal of this plan is a child who looks at every letter. Like this.

5
00:00:16.842 --> 00:00:17.857
The word is cap.

6
00:00:18.757 --> 00:00:24.445
That is the goal. It is not a promise. Day ten is a check, and it shows you where your child is.

7
00:00:25.245 --> 00:00:29.490
This video tells you what the plan is, what to expect, and how to use it.

8
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:35.226
This plan is for a child who knows most of the letter sounds, but guesses at words.

9
00:00:35.676 --> 00:00:38.809
Some children say a word that starts with the same letter.

10
00:00:39.259 --> 00:00:41.814
Some look at the picture, and say what it shows.

11
00:00:42.264 --> 00:00:46.911
And some know a whole book by heart, but cannot read the same words in a new place.

12
00:00:47.361 --> 00:00:51.908
It is common at five, six and seven. It is a habit, not a lack of effort.

13
00:00:52.358 --> 00:00:58.137
Guessing is quick, and in a book with a picture for every line, it often works. So the habit stays.

14
00:00:58.937 --> 00:01:03.441
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

15
00:01:03.891 --> 00:01:09.900
Day one is a short check. It shows you which guessing habit it is. Day ten shows you what changed.

16
00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:15.607
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

17
00:01:16.057 --> 00:01:19.961
And there are three moves. Each one takes away something a guess feeds on.

18
00:01:20.661 --> 00:01:24.946
Move one. Touch every letter. A finger under each one, from left to right.

19
00:01:25.396 --> 00:01:31.191
Move two. Cover and slide. A paper card hides the word, and shows one letter at a time.

20
00:01:31.641 --> 00:01:34.653
Like this. One letter. Then two. Then the whole word.

21
00:01:35.153 --> 00:01:37.426
The card is in the book, ready to cut out.

22
00:01:37.926 --> 00:01:42.888
Move three. The picture comes last. Read the word first. Look at the picture after.

23
00:01:43.688 --> 00:01:46.702
Now, what to expect. One small move at a time.

24
00:01:47.152 --> 00:01:52.681
Reading gets slower at first. That is the point. A child who guesses is going too fast.

25
00:01:53.131 --> 00:01:57.963
Some days will need a second try. Doing a page twice is not falling behind.

26
00:01:58.413 --> 00:02:01.442
On day ten, the check gives you one of three next steps.

27
00:02:02.242 --> 00:02:06.744
When a guess comes, do not say the word. Say the same five words, every time.

28
00:02:07.194 --> 00:02:09.652
Look again. Touch every letter. Then wait.

29
00:02:10.552 --> 00:02:17.039
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

30
00:02:17.489 --> 00:02:22.057
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps.

31
00:02:22.507 --> 00:02:25.654
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

32
00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:30.423
Then your child carries on with the page, and reads three things to you at the end.

33
00:02:30.873 --> 00:02:35.640
On four of the days there is a sound track for your child. You press play and step away.

34
00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:41.305
You need the printed pages, a pencil, crayons, and scissors for the slide card.

35
00:02:41.755 --> 00:02:46.844
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about four minutes.
